  "body": "Adds the optional Proxima control manifest, usage notes, and a Windows PowerShell validation harness. The harness validates a strict data-only manifest AST before importing the module, including rejection of executable blocks and background pipelines.\n\nExact head: `53b175c40254b0e64a011ef6d0f70207fd2f933e`. Packet #1285 r5/g6; Mission #1238. Three new files, 450 added lines. Existing S1/S2 files are byte-identical.\n\nValidation: Linux selftest 1777/1777; strict release verification 184/184; Ruff baseline delta 0. Focused native PS 5.1/7: normal 7/7, CX 12/12, unchanged S2 26/26; six AST negatives reject before import, with a private mutation proving the background-pipeline guard. Original native artifacts and independent source audit are retained in the Packet evidence.\n\nIndependent Codex CLI review approved the full base-to-head diff and closed F01: executor gpt-6.1-sol/high, fresh reviewer gpt-6.1-sol/xhigh, actual terminal identities measured. [Original verdict and validated v2 receipt](https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/issues/1285#issuecomment-6725935521). This is same-provider assurance.\n\nCH\u01afA \u0110\u1ee6 \u0110I\u1ec0U KI\u1ec6N MERGE: sensitive assurance still requires sufficient independent audit under protocol \u00a78; exact-head PR CI and connector review are pending. Keep Draft; no Ready, auto-merge, merge, land, or LIVE activation. Windows CI/full Windows mutant CI excluded by owner instruction; focused native Windows tests above were run.",
